.TH FERRET 1 "2026" "ferret 0.1.0-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferret, frt \- fast, byte-for-byte GNU find(1) clone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferret
.RI [ path ...]
.RI [ expression ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ferret
is a from-scratch C reimplementation of GNU
.BR find (1).
For a given expression and filesystem state its output matches GNU find 4.10.0
byte for byte, and it is faster on the workloads measured.
.PP
The man page is filled in as the predicate and action surface lands (sprint 11);
see the GNU
.BR find (1)
manual for the expression language.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
all operands processed successfully;
.B 1
an error occurred (a bad command line or a runtime failure on a file).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1)
.SH AUTHORS
The ferret authors.
